 "f2b286d5-0094-5d27-8122-cf59c572339d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0e94f97-83d4-55d1-a4fe-2eecc3c33c28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439943} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a071a57-c0a2-5ff5-8488-5bd97002af7b" :answer-field/key "VI" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440329} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7f8d1ef-4d2a-52c3-97a7-ce498c4ce11b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439945} {:answer/id #uuid "35e5554f-349d-51bb-9ccd-94b46e947c71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439946}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7f8d1ef-4d2a-52c3-97a7-ce498c4ce11b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439945} :answer-field/id #uuid "d02f2705-c6d5-5710-8589-44dd2b88e45c" :answer-field/key "VII" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440330}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5577e429-0d55-5dd4-b588-49ac727edd6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-72440" :question/problem "At which points on the curve ${x}^{2}+2xy=-5y+4$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $j?$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.\n\n- **I.** $(-4,1)$\n- **II.** $(-4,4)$\n- **III.** $(-2,4)$\n- **IV.** $(-1,1)$\n- **V.** $(-1,4)$\n- **VI.** $(1,1)$\n- **VII.** $(4,-4)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2xy & =-5y+4 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2xy+5y & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+2xy+5y$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=4.$ \n\nA tangent vector to the level curve can be computed as follows:\n\n$$\nt(x,y)={f}_{y}(x,y)\\,i-{f}_{x}(x,y)\\,j\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(x,y) & ={f}_{y}(x,y)\\,i-{f}_{x}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+2xy+5y)i-\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+2xy+5y)j \\\\  & =(2x+5)\\,i-(2x+2y)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nSince our tangent vector needs to be perpendicular to $j$, we must have $t\\cdot j=0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)\\cdot j & =0 \\\\ ((2x+5)\\,i-(2x+2y)\\,j)\\cdot j & =0 \\\\ -(2x+2y) & =0 \\\\ x & =-y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-y$ into the equation of our curve gives:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2xy+5y & =4 \\\\ (-y)^{2}+2(-y)y+5y & =4 \\\\ {y}^{2}-2{y}^{2}+5y & =4 \\\\ -{y}^{2}+5y-4 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}-5y+4 & =0 \\\\ (y-1)(y-4) & =0 \\\\ y & =1\\,\\text{or}\\,y=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally:\n\n- If $y=1$, we get $x=-1$ and the corresponding point is $(-1,1).$\n\n- If $y=4$, we get $x=-4$ and the corresponding point is $(-4,4).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532656 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152285 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84e87d0d-806d-5587-849e-17d6999dbbd1" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Second-Order IVPs When the Characteristic Equation Has Repeated Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20d48bb0-1579-5910-bda9-3488cfc27188" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{5x}-9x{e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531999} {:answer/id #uuid "364be568-53f5-599a-b8c5-5d41c25c736d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{5x}+6x{e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532042} {:answer/id #uuid "644ffb41-3a13-5e6e-829b-683cb23cf0e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{5x}+x{e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532155} {:answer/id #uuid "747e9c3b-3d01-5594-9408-b23ec8e2b378" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{5x}+3x{e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532197} {:answer/id #uuid "f20309b5-4187-58b6-b1e7-3989a23ea58e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{5x}+4x{e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532457}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "364be568-53f5-599a-b8c5-5d41c25c736d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{5x}+6x{e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532042} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f3de0d8-361d-5e2c-a8ff-302d31ec457a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532530}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "534aed09-ef02-5ca1-a426-154a43b90b94" :question/math-academy-id "q-94015" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-10{y}^{′}+25y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{5x}+Bx{e}^{5x},\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-10{y}^{′}+25y=0,\\,y(0)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=16.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA=2.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=16,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=5A{e}^{5x}+B{e}^{5x}+5Bx{e}^{5x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=16$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n5A+B=16.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $A=2$ gives $B=6.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=2{e}^{5x}+6x{e}^{5x}.\n$$"}]}
